WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.215 --> 00:00:02.400
&gt;&gt; Hey, there and welcome to the course.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.570
I'm Jessica Olman.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.950
&gt;&gt; And I'm Cameron Pittman.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.120
We're going to be your instructors for this course.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.244
&gt;&gt; Now, you're probably wondering why this course is

00:00:10.244 --> 00:00:13.021
called Not Your Typical Intro to HTML and CSS.

00:00:13.021 --> 00:00:15.793
That's because we're not going to show you how to

00:00:15.793 --> 00:00:18.713
make a web page with a title and some body to start.

00:00:18.713 --> 00:00:21.471
Instead, we're going to show you a methodical way of

00:00:21.471 --> 00:00:25.460
breaking down a current web page and recreating it for your own purposes.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.326
&gt;&gt; Hm, you know, HTML and CSS develop and change over time.

00:00:30.326 --> 00:00:32.820
But the underlying principles will always remain the same.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.319
Once you get a hang of those,

00:00:34.319 --> 00:00:37.704
learning the specific techniques is going to become a lot easier.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:41.773
In the first lesson, you'll learn how to look at a basic design mockup and

00:00:41.773 --> 00:00:44.810
translate it to HTML and CSS to create a basic web page.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.760
&gt;&gt; And in the second lesson, you'll develop a CSS framework,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.566
which will help you make websites much faster and easier.

00:00:52.566 --> 00:00:56.154
Along the way, you'll learn about responsive design, which is a principle that

00:00:56.154 --> 00:00:59.700
will help you reach people on any device that they're using to see your website.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.775
In the last lesson, you'll be taking on a professional framework.

00:01:03.775 --> 00:01:07.417
You'll be building a static website using Twitter's Bootstrap framework,

00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:11.000
which is what professionals use in the field every day.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.880
&gt;&gt; Now, this course is just the beginning of your journey to

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.600
become a front-end web developer.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.723
Here you'll build the foundations of your own online portfolio.

00:01:20.723 --> 00:01:22.630
&gt;&gt; We are really excited to have you.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:24.610
So, welcome to class and let's get started

